  "memo": "PDL BioPharma currently functions as a disparate collection of high-quality royalty assets trapped within a failing, cash-burning operating shell [D01, D06]. While management has finally acknowledged the need for change, their piecemeal approach to asset divestiture is a half-measure that threatens to leave shareholders with lingering overhead and continued value destruction [D05, D07]. The clinical failure of Nuvion underscores our conviction that the company should exit the drug-development business entirely rather than attempting to iterate on a flawed research strategy [D02].\n\nOur original thesis—that the market fails to distinguish between finite, high-margin royalty streams and the precarious economics of a laboratory-focused biotech—remains the core mispricing [D01, D06]. With the company's operating margin struggling and R&D spend remaining a significant drain on cash, the status quo is unacceptable [D02, D03, D06]. Any further delay in finalizing the sale of non-core assets or returning capital to shareholders serves only to consume the very cash we seek to protect [D03, D07].\n\nWe are escalating our involvement to ensure that the ongoing strategic review results in a complete separation of the royalty business from the commercial operating segment. We demand clear, binding terms for the divestitures and an explicit, immediate policy regarding the distribution of proceeds [D07]. We have no interest in watching management burn through cash on further development experiments; the path to value realization is the total liquidation of the commercial business and the maximization of the remaining royalty franchise [D05, D06].",
